+# Aegis Evidence Retention Policy (template)
+
+Purpose
+- Define storage, retention, and access controls for auditor evidence produced by Aegis (HIL bundles, formal artifacts, SLO proofs, builder evidence).
+
+Scope
+- Applies to all artifacts recorded with ops/sdk/evidence_sdk.record_manifest and auditor bundles produced by operator audit flows.
+
+Retention policy (example)
+- All signed auditor bundles (tar.gz + cosign signature) must be stored in s3://aegis-evidence/YYYY-MM-DD/<run-id>/ and retained for at least 365 days.
+- MLflow run artifacts and logs shall be retained for a minimum of 180 days.
+- Rekor/Signing metadata is permanent (kept as long as Rekor server retains entries).
+
+Access & encryption
+- Evidence S3 buckets must enforce server-side encryption and IAM policies that restrict access to Platform Owner and Safety Officer roles.
+
+Deletion & legal hold
+- Deletion of evidence requires Platform Owner approval and must record an auditable deletion manifest.
+- Legal hold supersedes retention; records under legal hold must not be deleted.
+
+Review cadence
+- Monthly review of evidence storage and retention compliance; annual audit to validate retention controls.
+
