+# Aegis Operator Runbook (detailed)
+
+Sections:
+- Roles & contacts
+- Preflight checks before audit run
+- How to run the complete audit
+- How to interpret RT SLO proof & HIL outputs
+- How to submit bundle to certifier
+- Emergency escalation & revocation steps
+
+Preflight checks
+1. Ensure COSIGN_KMS_URI and REKOR_SERVER are configured in CI and locally (export as env vars).  
+2. Ensure WATTTIME_API_KEY for carbon gating is available (if gating used).  
+3. Ensure self-hosted runners are labeled correctly (gpu, inferentia, graphcore, habana).  
+4. Ensure S3 evidence bucket accessible and operator account has write permissions.
+
+Running a full audit
+1. Execute: ./ops/operator/run_complete_audit.sh --node <robot-host> --out /tmp/audit_run --s3 s3://aegis-evidence/<run-id>  
+2. Wait for script completion; the script will sign the bundle with COSIGN_KMS_URI (if provided).  
+3. Inspect the bundle and index file at <out>/index.json (if present) and rt_slo_proof.json.
+
+Interpreting RT SLO proof
+- Open ops/robotics/rt/lab_validation/rt_slo_prover.py output (rt_slo_proof.json). Check p99_ok and safe_ok booleans.  
+- If either false: review jitter sample sets and safe_stop traces in the bundle and investigate controller loop load and IRQ/NIC settings.
+
+Submitting to a certifier
+1. Upload bundle to secure channel or S3 as agreed with certifier. Include cosign signature and Rekor entries.  
+2. Attach this cover letter (ops/governance/auditor_cover_letter.md) and HARA / test_matrix.csv.
+
+Emergency escalation
+- If SLO breach in production: immediately disable actuator action via approval service and run safe-stop procedures. Notify Safety Officer and Controls Lead.
